Item 01 is done. Everything is written: the harness, the run, the report section, the tests, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md. No commit was made, nothing was written to `solutions/`, and no solver default or C code changed.

**The harness found what it was built to find.** Over 43,935 certified instances at 9 to 40 customers, ten labellings each, both configurations and both sides of the optimum, every refutation at `optimum − 1` held on all 878,580 calls and the lattice oracle agreed on all 13,612 instances it reaches. But at `k = optimum`, where a witness exists, the C search with Theorem 2 on answered `unsat` 88 times on 56 instances. All 56 stored optima re-certify by independent routes, so the values are right and the rule is wrong.

**Mechanism.** `better_move` alone is sound on all 88 cases. Composed with `subset_rule` (78) or `definite_move` (3) it forms a cross-rule dominance cycle: `subset_rule` runs after `better_move` and measures survivors against candidates `better_move` has just discarded, so two customers each get dropped on the strength of the other. This is the same failure shape as the 2026-09-23 `better_move` bug, now arising between rules rather than within one. The report proposes a fix and does not apply it.

**Alert for the owner.** The failing configuration is what `benchmarks.csearch` used and what the running `benchmarks.recertify` uses on the 125×125 instances. At `n ≤ 40` no stored value is affected. Above 40 nothing here is evidence, and the `default` search cannot check those sizes. I did not stop recertify.

**Other deliverables.** The relabelling spread by size band and configuration is recorded for item 04: at `n ≤ 40` a best-of-nine portfolio gains nothing on refutations and 16 to 17% on witness searches. The §13 re-covering invariants hold on all 43,935 instances.

Files: `learning/differential.py`, `tests/test_differential.py` (11 pass, one strict xfail that flips when the C is fixed), `reports/ml_nature.md` §15, `reports/differential_tables.md`, four CSVs under `learning/data/ensemble/` (11 MB). Full suite: 824 passed, 2 skipped, 2 xfailed.

